messages she gives us are all short, only two or three paragraphs.

224
00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:56.760
When you go up into the higher volumes, you can have three or four A4 pages for one message.

225
00:20:56.760 --> 00:21:03.600
So Louisa has been liberated to be able to express the divine things on paper.

226
00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:11.160
But we won't jump because we need to take that journey step-by-step together.

227
00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:19.640
So April the 21st, 1900, and again we're talking about the cross.

228
00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:25.680
Have you noticed that when a subject comes up, you very often get a number of messages

229
00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:30.720
all on the same theme?

230
00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:36.080
As I was in my usual state, Louisa said, or rather a little bit of concern about something

231
00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:38.880
which is not necessary to say here.

232
00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:45.360
"Sweet Jesus on coming said to me, 'And they are sacred vessels,' he said.

233
00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:48.560
And every once in a while it is necessary to dust them off.

234
00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:51.240
Now Louisa's starting in the middle of a sentence.

235
00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:56.000
Whatever Jesus said before this, we don't know, because she didn't write it down.

236
00:21:56.000 --> 00:22:02.720
The only point at which he began to write is when Jesus said, 'And they are sacred vessels.'

237
00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:06.120
And every once in a while it is necessary to dust them off.

238
00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:10.160
Now he says, 'Your bodies are as many sacred vessels.'

239
00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:21.640
That's one Corinthians 3, 16, and two Corinthians 6, 16, 'In which I make my dwelling, therefore

240
00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:27.360
it is necessary that I do some dusting every now and then.'

241
00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:31.560
That means we need continuous purification.

242
00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:42.680
And Jesus said, 'He dusts us when he visits us with some tribulation so that I may remain

243
00:22:42.680 --> 00:22:47.380
in them with more decorum, therefore become.'

244
00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:52.880
In other words, purification has got to go on continuously because we cannot imagine the

245
00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:58.440
humiliation it is for the Lord to come and dwell in us things of flesh.

246
00:22:58.440 --> 00:23:00.320
We just can't imagine it.

247
00:23:00.320 --> 00:23:03.440
So I want to give you Philippians 3, 18 for that.

248
00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:09.680
'Later after I received communion, having renewed in me the pains of the crucifixion

249
00:23:09.680 --> 00:23:16.360
Jesus added, my daughter, how precious the cross is.'

250
00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:25.160
See now, in giving itself to the soul, the sacrament of my body unites her with me.

251
00:23:25.160 --> 00:23:32.320
It transforms her to the point that she becomes one with me.

252
00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:38.720
But as the species is consumed, which is only fifteen minutes, the union which is truly

253
00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:45.160
established ceases, but not with the cross.

254
00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:53.960
The cross takes God and unites him with the soul forever, and it places itself more surely

255
00:23:53.960 --> 00:23:56.080
as a seal.

256
00:23:56.080 --> 00:24:01.280
Therefore, the cross seals God in the soul.

257
00:24:01.280 --> 00:24:04.400
Isn't that absolutely amazing?

258
00:24:04.400 --> 00:24:11.320
In such a way that there is never separation between God and the crucified soul.

259
00:24:11.320 --> 00:24:19.480
Now, the crucified soul is the one who is completely given to him and continues moment

260
00:24:19.480 --> 00:24:27.200
by moment, hour by hour, day by day, continuously giving itself to him, giving itself, giving

261
00:24:27.200 --> 00:24:33.400
itself, giving itself, sacrificing itself for love, sacrificing itself for love all the

262
00:24:33.400 --> 00:24:34.880
time.

263
00:24:34.880 --> 00:24:42.360
So divine will and love is the essence of what God has asked us to enter into.

264
00:24:42.360 --> 00:24:48.400
So April the 23rd, 1900, he comes back to talk about resignation.

265
00:24:48.400 --> 00:24:54.040
But he says it's like oil that is a salve for the body.

266
00:24:54.040 --> 00:24:59.600
So finding this morning, finding myself outside of myself, I saw my sweet Jesus suffering

267
00:24:59.600 --> 00:25:02.240
very much.

268
00:25:02.240 --> 00:25:07.320
And I prayed him to share his pains with me and he said, "You too suffer.

269
00:25:07.320 --> 00:25:13.880
Rather, I will take your place and you will do for me the office of a nurse."

270
00:25:13.880 --> 00:25:21.440
Now, in volume two, he asked her to be a second mother for him on the earth so that he often

271
00:25:21.440 --> 00:25:27.720
comes to her as an infant and asks her to do ministry to him.

272
00:25:27.720 --> 00:25:36.800
And that simply is an illustration of, or shall I say, an explanation as to what her

273
00:25:36.800 --> 00:25:43.040
ministry is in intercession and as a victim soul.

274
00:25:43.040 --> 00:25:45.000
So now she's asked to be a nurse.

275
00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:49.080
So it seemed that Jesus placed himself in my bed and I beside him began to check his

276
00:25:49.080 --> 00:25:53.120
head, removing the thorns that were driven into it one by one.

277
00:25:53.120 --> 00:25:57.280
Then I moved on to his body and visited all his wounds.

278
00:25:57.280 --> 00:26:05.760
I dried up his blood, I kissed them, but I had nothing with me to salve them so as to

279
00:26:05.760 --> 00:26:07.800
mitigate the spasm.

280
00:26:07.800 --> 00:26:16.600
When I saw that oil was coming out from me, I took it and I salved the wounds of Jesus.

281
00:26:16.600 --> 00:26:21.240
But with some concern, as I didn't understand what the meaning was of this oil coming out

282
00:26:21.240 --> 00:26:26.360
of me, we'll talk about the oil first.

283
00:26:26.360 --> 00:26:33.320
But blessed Jesus made me understand that resignation to the divine will is the oil, which while

284
00:26:33.320 --> 00:26:39.320
salving and mitigating our pains, salves and mitigates the spasms of the wounds of Jesus

285
00:26:39.320 --> 00:26:41.520
at the same time.

286
00:26:41.520 --> 00:26:48.040
Because resignation cams and heals us from the agitation that we had beforehand.

287
00:26:48.040 --> 00:26:51.840
Then after performing this office of my dear Jesus for quite some time, he disappeared

288
00:26:51.840 --> 00:26:54.000
and I came back to myself.

289
00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:58.200
Now you may wonder what on earth she's doing to the body of Christ.

290
00:26:58.200 --> 00:27:05.600
But if you go into the hours of the passion, you have in the agony in the garden, you

291
00:27:05.600 --> 00:27:12.960
have after the creation of the Eucharist and you have around the cross.

292
00:27:12.960 --> 00:27:18.280
And she goes through all the wounds of Jesus making reparation, making reparation, making

293
00:27:18.280 --> 00:27:19.640
reparation.

294
00:27:19.640 --> 00:27:23.040
And she loves him for everyone in the divine will.

295
00:27:23.040 --> 00:27:28.760
And she kisses him for everybody in the divine will and she offers reparation for all the

296
00:27:28.760 --> 00:27:31.480
wounds from head to toe.

297
00:27:31.480 --> 00:27:37.280
So that's what you're getting here in picture form.

298
00:27:37.280 --> 00:27:42.960
April the 24th, 1900, the Eucharist and suffering.

299
00:27:42.960 --> 00:27:48.160
This morning, having received communion, Louise said, it seemed to me that the confessor was

300
00:27:48.160 --> 00:27:53.380
placing the intention of making me suffer the crucifixion.

301
00:27:53.380 --> 00:27:59.320
And at that very instant, I saw my guardian angel who laid me on the cross to make me

302
00:27:59.320 --> 00:28:01.520
suffer.

303
00:28:01.520 --> 00:28:06.920
Now most of us don't think that the guardian angel will do that particular function.

304
00:28:06.920 --> 00:28:14.760
But if you go to the prophet Daniel in the Old Testament, they prophet Ezekiel in the

305
00:28:14.760 --> 00:28:22.120
Old Testament and the book of Revelation in the New Testament just to give you three examples.

306
00:28:22.120 --> 00:28:30.320
You will find that it is the angels who always carry out God's will upon the earth.

307
00:28:30.320 --> 00:28:35.200
So Louise's guardian angel laid her on the cross and made her suffer.

308
00:28:35.200 --> 00:28:41.600
After this, she said, I saw my sweet Jesus who sympathized with me and told me, I am

309
00:28:41.600 --> 00:28:46.800
your refreshment and my refreshment is your suffering for souls.

310
00:28:46.800 --> 00:28:53.760
Now, that suffering for souls, of course, is the reparation that the victim soul does

311
00:28:53.760 --> 00:28:55.760
and does it out of love.

312
00:28:55.760 --> 00:29:03.000
So notice that this is reciprocal love from Jesus to the soul and vice versa.

313
00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:08.220
And he showed an unspeakable contentment for my suffering and for the confessor who by

314
00:29:08.220 --> 00:29:15.640
means of the obedience to suffer which he had given me had procured this relief for him.

315
00:29:15.640 --> 00:29:23.200
Then he added, since the sacrament of the Eucharist is the flute of the cross, I feel

316
00:29:23.200 --> 00:29:28.760
more disposed to concede suffering to you after you receive my body.

317
00:29:28.760 --> 00:29:35.680
So you will have noticed from the very beginning that it's after Louise has received Holy Communion

318
00:29:35.680 --> 00:29:40.420
that these communications about suffering take place.

319
00:29:40.420 --> 00:29:46.140
In fact, in seeing you suffer, it seems to me, Jesus said, that I continue my passion

320
00:29:46.140 --> 00:29:52.520
on the earth for the good of souls, not mystically, in other words, not in some very very place,

321
00:29:52.520 --> 00:29:59.760
but really it's actually happening.

322
00:29:59.760 --> 00:30:06.940
And this is a great relief for me because I collect the true fruit of the cross and of

323
00:30:06.940 --> 00:30:08.400
the Eucharist.

324
00:30:08.400 --> 00:30:14.360
So here you have Louise representing the body of Christ, going through the passion of Christ

325
00:30:14.360 --> 00:30:16.000
on the earth.

326
00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:20.920
And she can only do it bit by bit because after all, she's only a little creature.

327
00:30:20.920 --> 00:30:26.360
Jesus was able to take it all at the same time.

328
00:30:26.360 --> 00:30:33.720
After this Jesus said, "Up until now, it was obedience that made you suffer.

329
00:30:33.720 --> 00:30:39.480
Do you want me to enjoy myself a little bit by renewing again in you the crucifixion with

330
00:30:39.480 --> 00:30:41.640
my own hands?"

331
00:30:41.640 --> 00:30:45.960
In other words, would you actually let me do it?

332
00:30:45.960 --> 00:30:58.280
And Louise said, "Though I felt great suffering and still fresh the pains of the cross which

333
00:30:58.280 --> 00:31:04.800
had been renewed in me, she said, 'I said, 'Lord, I'm in your hands.

334
00:31:04.800 --> 00:31:06.480
Do with me whatever you want.'"

335
00:31:06.480 --> 00:31:12.200
So that's like the Fiat of Blessed Mother in Luke 1.38.

336
00:31:12.200 --> 00:31:15.680
Be it done unto me according to your word.

337
00:31:15.680 --> 00:31:21.960
So all content, Jesus again began to drive the nails into my hands and feet.

338
00:31:21.960 --> 00:31:28.160
I felt such intensity of pain that I myself do not know how I remained alive, but I was

339
00:31:28.160 --> 00:31:33.440
content because I was making Jesus content.

340
00:31:33.440 --> 00:31:43.880
Then after he bent the nails, placing himself near me, he said, "How beautiful you are."

341
00:31:43.880 --> 00:31:47.880
But how much more does your beauty grow in suffering?

342
00:31:47.880 --> 00:31:54.200
In other words, he's talking about interior beauty or how dear you are to me.

343
00:31:54.200 --> 00:32:01.080
My eyes are wounded and looking at you because they see my very image in you.

344
00:32:01.080 --> 00:32:04.520
That's Romans 8.29.

345
00:32:04.520 --> 00:32:08.360
And he said many other things which would be useless to repeat first because I'm bad.

346
00:32:08.360 --> 00:32:13.680
She said, "A second because not seeing myself as the Lord tells me.

347
00:32:13.680 --> 00:32:18.460
I feel confusion and blushing in saying these things, but I hope that the Lord will make

348
00:32:18.460 --> 00:32:20.240
me truly good and beautiful.

349
00:32:20.240 --> 00:32:25.560
And then as my blushing would fade, I will be able to distribute them so I stop here.

350
00:32:25.560 --> 00:32:28.840
I want to give you Galatians 2.19.

351
00:32:28.840 --> 00:32:33.320
Now there's a mystery here.

352
00:32:33.320 --> 00:32:39.000
Louisa is suffering the passion and she's allowed to suffer it just for a short time.

353
00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:44.080
And that's because of the weakness of human flesh, otherwise we would kill her.

354
00:32:44.080 --> 00:32:51.320
And then Jesus comes along and he says, "Would you like me to enjoy myself by giving you

355
00:32:51.320 --> 00:32:54.440
the crucifixion myself?

356
00:32:54.440 --> 00:32:57.720
That we really need to think about this."

357
00:32:57.720 --> 00:33:04.920
Because when we think of the crucifixion of Christ, we have this image of the baddies

358
00:33:04.920 --> 00:33:11.840
in Israel hating Jesus and causing him all kinds of terrifying pains and we have that

359
00:33:11.840 --> 00:33:16.600
baddie pilot who is condemning him on jostly and blah, blah, blah.

360
00:33:16.600 --> 00:33:24.120
And we don't realize that none of that could have happened if Jesus hadn't willed it and

361
00:33:24.120 --> 00:33:31.000
if Jesus hadn't actually surrendered his divine power and if Jesus hadn't surrendered

362
00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:39.520
to them and that he wanted this suffering in order to be able to show us the utter limits

363
00:33:39.520 --> 00:33:42.160
of love.

364
00:33:42.160 --> 00:33:48.240
In order to be able to show us that as far as God is concerned, God would do anything

365
00:33:48.240 --> 00:33:50.400
to save us.

366
00:33:50.400 --> 00:33:57.400
He would do anything to let us know that he considered us very precious.

367
00:33:57.400 --> 00:34:04.520
And to let us know that God is completely different to what we think, that God himself

368
00:34:04.520 --> 00:34:08.520
wanted to pay this infinite debt.

369
00:34:08.520 --> 00:34:10.200
It's just amazing.

370
00:34:10.200 --> 00:34:15.200
You know the parable about the unforgiving debtor.

371
00:34:15.200 --> 00:34:20.480
That unforgiving debtor represents every sinner that ever lived.

372
00:34:20.480 --> 00:34:26.780
And when we commit a sin, we're sinning against an infinite being, therefore the debt is infinite.

373
00:34:26.780 --> 00:34:32.080
And therefore just as you're told in the parable that no matter what the man did or suffered,

374
00:34:32.080 --> 00:34:35.280
he could never ever pay the debt.

375
00:34:35.280 --> 00:34:42.840
So the only chance he had of anything was to throw himself at the mercy of a king who

376
00:34:42.840 --> 00:34:45.880
was going to condemn him.

377
00:34:45.880 --> 00:34:51.320
And the moment he throws himself at the mercy of the king, he gets instant and absolute

378
00:34:51.320 --> 00:34:53.240
forgiveness.

379
00:34:53.240 --> 00:34:59.160
Now you would expect this person to suffer from some kind of psychological shock.

380
00:34:59.160 --> 00:35:03.320
One minute I'm being sold in slavery myself, my wife and my children, to try and pay a

381
00:35:03.320 --> 00:35:09.120
debt that I can't pay, and all of a sudden I'm free.

382
00:35:09.120 --> 00:35:15.840
And so you're completely and totally shocked when the man doesn't even say, gee, thanks.

383
00:35:15.840 --> 00:35:18.240
There's no gratitude in him.

384
00:35:18.240 --> 00:35:25.240
There's no humility in him, there's no love in him, and he shows this by maltreating one

385
00:35:25.240 --> 00:35:27.640
of his fellow servants.

386
00:35:27.640 --> 00:35:35.920
So the unforgiving debtor is us because throughout these writings, Jesus identifies the human

387
00:35:35.920 --> 00:35:43.680
race as the ungrateful one, the one who does not appreciate what was done for them, does

388
00:35:43.680 --> 00:35:52.600
not say thank you, does not take the gift and let it do the work that it can do in us.

389
00:35:52.600 --> 00:35:57.040
And so it's a terrible picture of us.

390
00:35:57.040 --> 00:36:07.880
And so when Jesus says to Louisa, can I actually get you to participate in this mystery from

391
00:36:07.880 --> 00:36:14.280
me, he's talking about the fact that Louisa explains in the agony, in the garden, in

392
00:36:14.280 --> 00:36:19.320
the hours of the passion, that Jesus suffered a passion of love given to him directly by

393
00:36:19.320 --> 00:36:27.000
the father, the passion of sin given by us, and then what she calls the passion of the

394
00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:32.160
Jews, in other words, what human beings did to him in the crucifixion.

395
00:36:32.160 --> 00:36:36.160
But the worst passion was the passion of love.

396
00:36:36.160 --> 00:36:41.360
The second worst one was the passion of sin that made him sweat blood.

397
00:36:41.360 --> 00:36:42.360
Okay.

398
00:36:42.360 --> 00:36:50.160
So Jesus is asking Louisa to participate in this extraordinary mystery, that she would

399
00:36:50.160 --> 00:36:57.360
allow the passion of love to happen, and therefore she would be very, very, very much in the

400
00:36:57.360 --> 00:36:59.120
image of Jesus.

401
00:36:59.120 --> 00:37:06.040
That's what's causing him joy, that somebody else is willing to give this sign to the father

402
00:37:06.040 --> 00:37:13.240
that they love God beyond reason, and they love their neighbor beyond reason as well.

403
00:37:13.240 --> 00:37:17.600
So it's a wonderful thing that's happening there.

404
00:37:17.600 --> 00:37:23.040
That's why he tells her how beautiful you are, and your beauty grows in suffering.

405
00:37:23.040 --> 00:37:27.120
It's because of this unbelievable love that's behind it.

406
00:37:27.120 --> 00:37:28.120
Okay.

407
00:37:28.120 --> 00:37:34.520
So let's go on to April the 25th, 1900, where we talk about purity of intention.

408
00:37:34.520 --> 00:37:42.960
Now, this is one of the vital lessons in volumes one to four, that we are told that we must

409
00:37:42.960 --> 00:37:45.160
have purity of intention.

410
00:37:45.160 --> 00:37:51.800
That means you have only one reason for doing something, and the only intention that's accepted

411
00:37:51.800 --> 00:37:57.320
in the divine will spirituality is that you do everything for love of Jesus.

412
00:37:57.320 --> 00:38:02.040
Let me give you an example of an intention that's not pure.

413
00:38:02.040 --> 00:38:07.000
More means unmixed with something else.

414
00:38:07.000 --> 00:38:08.480
Okay.

415
00:38:08.480 --> 00:38:12.840
Virgin means untouched by something else.

416
00:38:12.840 --> 00:38:18.520
So let me give you an example of impurity of intention.

417
00:38:18.520 --> 00:38:24.760
So I tell my friends and my family that I'm going to fast for a few days, you know, and

418
00:38:24.760 --> 00:38:28.840
everybody says, "Oh, isn't she so religious, isn't it fantastic, you know, she's doing

419
00:38:28.840 --> 00:38:32.320
this incredible thing that we couldn't do," and blah, blah, blah.

420
00:38:32.320 --> 00:38:35.640
But in the back of my head, I'm saying to myself, "But I could lose a few pounds as

421
00:38:35.640 --> 00:38:36.640
well."

422
00:38:36.640 --> 00:38:43.360
Now, it's that thought in the back of my head that makes the whole thing impure and makes

423
00:38:43.360 --> 00:38:50.120
the fasting of no value whatsoever, there's poison in the intention.

424
00:38:50.120 --> 00:38:57.440
I get that clearly, and you'll understand why Jesus comes back time after time to tell

425
00:38:57.440 --> 00:39:02.960
us that we must have purity of intention, that we do something for one reason only,

426
00:39:02.960 --> 00:39:05.680
and that one reason is to love Jesus.

427
00:39:05.680 --> 00:39:10.960
If you want to see this very clearly, you'll see it in the writings of Saint Therese of

428
00:39:10.960 --> 00:39:18.440
Lesus, where she continuously says she's doing everything for love of Jesus, for Jesus alone,

429
00:39:18.440 --> 00:39:19.440
for love of Jesus.

430
00:39:19.440 --> 00:39:21.880
No matter what it is, she's doing it for love of Him.

431
00:39:21.880 --> 00:39:25.920
You repent for love of Him, you serve your neighbor for love of Him, you deny yourself

432
00:39:25.920 --> 00:39:31.000
for love of Him, you pray for love of Him, you do everything for Him.

433
00:39:31.000 --> 00:39:35.320
So this is April the 25th, 1900.

434
00:39:35.320 --> 00:39:40.000
As I was in my usual state and not finding my sweet Jesus, I had to go around very much

435
00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:41.800
to go and search of Him.

436
00:39:41.800 --> 00:39:50.200
Finally, I found Him in the arms of our Queen Mother, suckling milk from her breasts.

437
00:39:50.200 --> 00:39:54.680
As much as I said and did, He did not seem to pay attention to me what child would pay

438
00:39:54.680 --> 00:40:00.600
attention to you when they are receiving life from their mothers.

439
00:40:00.600 --> 00:40:06.560
Who can say the pain of my poor heart in seeing Jesus and not paying attention to me?

440
00:40:06.560 --> 00:40:13.040
Then after I gave vent to my tears, having compassion on me, he came into my arms and

441
00:40:13.040 --> 00:40:20.640
poured from his mouth a little bit of that milk which he had suckled from his mother.

442
00:40:20.640 --> 00:40:25.360
Now look at the cycle of life that's going on here.

443
00:40:25.360 --> 00:40:29.160
The milk went from her to Him and from Him to Louisa.

